INSERT INTO memories VALUES(1,'global',NULL,'MCP tool availability is PERSONA-SCOPED (OpenWorker, as of 2026-08-20). A persona''s manifest `mcp:` list decides which of the 12 gateway servers it gets; `mcp: [none]` means none. Current profiles: research -> arxiv, tavily, context7, exa. repo-ops -> github, filesystem, qdrant, arxiv. fastchat -> none (kept lean: the full 12-server surface costs ~16k prompt tokens and 90s of prompt processing per turn on the local 27B model). IMPORTANT HISTORY: before 2026-08-20 scheduled automations had NO MCP tools at all — `prepare_mcp_tools` was only called from the WebSocket handler, so a scheduled run naming `arxiv-search_papers` or `qdrant-qdrant-store` was calling tools it could not see and silently fell back to shell/curl. That is now wired into `_run_scheduled_task`. If a tool call fails with ''unknown tool'', check the persona''s `mcp:` list first — the server is probably just not in this profile. GATEWAY CREDENTIAL STATE: as of 2026-08-24 the gateway''s github server token is BROKEN — `github-list_commits` returns `MCP error -32603: Authentication Failed: Bad credentials`, reverting the 9 private iconbaypark2900 repos to 404 for the repo-activity automation (last verified working 2026-08-20). Until the token is refreshed, repo-activity brief coverage is effectively 1/10 (only liaison-agentSystem).','MCP tools are persona-scoped; repo-ops has github+filesystem+qdrant+arxiv. NOTE 2026-08-24: gateway github token broken ("Bad credentials") — 9 private repos 404 again, 1/10 coverage until refreshed.',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-16 17:53:33');
INSERT INTO memories VALUES(2,'workspace',NULL,'9 of the 10 repos in the iconbaypark2900 "Repo activity brief" automation (dcode-stack, workstation-stack, ragtradesystem, sigma, qgg_research, materialScience, setup, polymarket_btc, sourcelab_ai_production_scaffold) are PRIVATE; only liaison-agentSystem is public. No GITHUB_TOKEN/GH_TOKEN or gh auth exists in the OpenWorker shell, so those 9 always 404 and cannot be reported on. Fix = set a token in env. Discovered 2026-08-19.','9 of 10 activity-brief repos are private, unauth''d GitHub access is all we have','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-717e4360ea',NULL,'2026-08-20 20:37:03');
INSERT INTO memories VALUES(3,'workspace',NULL,'The grant/funding digest workspace (resume.txt for Jonathan Beale) already contains grants-2026-week-33.md from a prior run (verified 2026-08-20). This digest is a scheduled weekly job; prior digests accumulate as grants-YYYY-week-WW.md. New digests should reference/update rather than duplicate prior weeks'' findings, and closed programs already covered can be briefly carried forward.','Digest runs accumulate weekly files; week-33 digest already existed','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-092a6d85f2',NULL,'2026-08-20 21:13:01');
INSERT INTO memories VALUES(4,'workspace',NULL,'In the "Repo activity brief" automation, 9 of the 10 repos (dcode-stack, workstation-stack, ragtradesystem, sigma, qgg_research, materialScience, setup, polymarket_btc, sourcelab_ai_production_scaffold) are PRIVATE under iconbaypark2900; only liaison-agentSystem is public. No GITHUB_TOKEN/GH_TOKEN is set in the OpenWorker shell, so those 9 cannot be queried (404 on API). Fix: add a token to the environment.','Repo brief: 9 repos private, no GH token, only liaison-agentSystem readable','/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-717e4360ea',NULL,'2026-08-20 21:53:47');
INSERT INTO memories VALUES(5,'global',NULL,replace('Qdrant (localhost:6333, v1.19.0, collection `default`, named vector `fast-all-minilm-l6-v2`, 384-dim cosine). PREFER THE MCP TOOLS: `qdrant-qdrant-store` and `qdrant-qdrant-find` handle embedding and the vector naming for you and are verified working (2026-08-20: a find for ''quantum error correction decoder'' returned correct hits). Do not hand-roll HTTP unless those are unavailable.\nCORRECTION to the earlier note, which was a misdiagnosis of standard Qdrant semantics, not a broken build:\n  * Upsert is PUT /collections/{c}/points with {"points":[{id, vector:{"<name>":[...]}, payload}]}. POST on that path is not an upsert endpoint at all — that is why it looked like a silent no-op shim.\n  * Vector search WORKS. For a NAMED vector the body must be the named-vector form: POST /points/search {"vector":{"name":"fast-all-minilm-l6-v2","vector":[...]},"limit":n}. A plain array or a top-level "using" field both fail with ''Not existing vector name''. The 1.11+ API also works: POST /points/query {"query":[...],"using":"<name>","limit":n}. Verified 2026-08-20 against the live 16-point collection.','\n',char(10)),'Local Qdrant: POST upsert silently no-ops; must use PUT with modern points body; search endpoint rejects all shapes',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 23:48:20');
INSERT INTO memories VALUES(6,'global',NULL,'User stated (2026-08-20): wants to build an open-source, Claude-Science-class stack combining OpenEvolve (AlphaEvolve-style evolutionary coding agent, GitHub algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve) with quantum chemistry for drug discovery + materials science. Components in play: OpenEvolve as optimization loop, open structure models (Boltz-2/Chai-1/ESMFold), RFdiffusion+ProteinMPNN design, PySCF/Psi4/ML-potential scoring, RDKit. Explicit goal: match Anthropic''s Claude Science polish — unified workflow over fragmented tools, auditable artifacts/provenance, flexible compute. Treat OpenEvolve/QM/drug-discovery questions as this ongoing project, not one-off help.','Building open Claude-Science-class OpenEvolve+QM stack for drug discovery and materials',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-21 01:27:45');
INSERT INTO memories VALUES(7,'workspace',NULL,'opensciencelab repo (branch phase2-drug-and-materials, ~/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab): as of 2026-08-25, Phase 2 fully closed (baseline 5bb839c) and Phase 3 in code COMPLETE — item 1 descriptors (6f71a30, local ref tip), item 2 Vina adapter (2529fa0) + 8ae4493 tier-billing fix, item 3 PySCF DFT, item 4 CHGNet. Working tree has descriptors.py, docking.py, dft.py, chgnet.py; suite was 71→85→97 tests across the items. CAVEAT: host lacks vina binary, RDKit/meeko, CHGNet — real-kernel paths only proven via fake-binary seam; live runs fall back to stamped surrogates. (Supersedes the 08-24 state of items 1/3/4 open.)','opensciencelab Phase 3 complete in code; live paths unverified on host.','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace',NULL,'2026-08-23 19:58:24');
