INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('7d62acc4-754','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','auto','Phase 2, item 3 only. Read PHASE2.md first (it records items','builder',274,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'I''ll start by reading the key files to understand the curren',0,'2026-08-23 12:53:31','{}','{"boundary_index": 169, "summary_text": "# 1. Primary request and intent\n\nImplement **Phase 2, item 3** of `openevolve_roadmap.md`: the **budget ledger** for `evolve()` calls. Every `evolve()` must:\n1. **Predict cost up front** (an honest upper bound from declared `max_evals`/`population`/`iterations` \u00d7 per-tier rate from `Budget.costs`), available *before* the search runs so a call that cannot fit in remaining budget fails fast with `BudgetExceeded`.\n2. **Count actual evaluations performed per tier** and report them in `Bundle.cost` so `Adapter.run` charges them.\n3. **Record the delta** (actual \u2212 predicted) on the Bundle and in the manifest.\n\n**Standing constraints:**\n- Domain-agnostic: nothing in `adapters/` may branch on molecules vs materials.\n- No new dependencies.\n- Do not regress the `notes` provenance stamps reaching `scored.jsonl` and manifest (item 2''s fix).\n- Do not touch `preflight.py` (item 4).\n- Do not fix the snapshot/digest issue (known-adjacent, deferred).\n- If an example trips the budget, that is the fix working \u2014 give it an explicit budget or smaller `max_evals` and document cost in PHASE2.md.\n- Commit work separately on branch `phase2-drug-and-materials`.\n- Use `/usr/bin/python3 -m pytest -q opensciencelab/tests.py` (conda python has no pytest).\n- Both example scripts must still run and print fronts.\n- Show proof: non-zero `budget` block + `calls[].cost` from a fresh run directory.\n- Update PHASE2.md with what item 3 does, what''s left, and anything found but not fixed.\n- Then stop.\n\n# 2. Key concepts and decisions\n\n- **The defect (original):** `adapters/optimize/adapter.py` returned hardcoded `cost = {0: 0.0, 1: 0.0, 2: 0.0}` in both `_exec` and `_hill_climb`, so Budget.spent stayed at zero.\n- **Architecture (implemented):**\n  - `Bundle` (base.py) carries `cost: Dict[int, float]`, `predicted_cost: Dict[int, float]`, `delta_cost: Dict[int, float]` + `total_cost()`.\n  - `Adapter` ABC now declares `predict_cost(inputs, budget) -> Dict[int, float]` as a concrete (non-abstract) method returning `{}` by default.\n  - `Adapter.run()` in base.py: (1) calls `self.predict_cost(inputs, budget)` to get the quote, (2) checks `budget.remaining_for(tier, amount)` for each tier in the quote (raises `BudgetExceeded` if insufficient), (3) calls `self._exec(...)`, (4) charges actual via `budget.spend(tier, amount)`, (5) calls `manifest.record(...)` with `cost`, `predicted_cost`, and `delta_cost`.\n  - The optimize adapter''s `_exec` and `_hill_climb` now use a `charge(tier, n)` closure that accumulates per-tier eval counts into `bundle_cost` dict; final `Bundle.cost` reflects real evals.\n  - `predict_cost` on the optimize adapter: `max_evals * rate(tier)` for the charged tier (one tier per call).\n  - `predict_cost` on scoring adapters: `n_candidates * rate(tier)` at their respective tiers.\n- **Budget (manifest.py):** `remaining_for(tier, amount)` is the pre-flight check (raises `BudgetExceeded`). `spend(tier, amount)` does the post-hoc charge. `budget_default()` caps tier-1 at 1000, tier-2 at 500; tier-0 uncapped.\n- **Design decision:** Predicted cost is an **upper bound**. Actual will routinely land **under** predicted because `_hill_climb` exits early on `plateau >= plateau_patience`. The delta records this gap; do not tune it away.\n- **Field name:** The Bundle field is `delta_cost` (NOT `cost_delta`) \u2014 confirmed by reading the dataclass at lines 124\u2013158.\n- **Adapter class name:** The class in adapter.py is `OpenEvolveAdapter` (registered in `__init__.py` line 64). An `OptimizeAdapter` reference appeared in a `_rate` static method but the actual class is `OpenEvolveAdapter`.\n- **Charging in `_hill_climb`:** A `charge(score_vec)` closure inspects `score_vec.tier` and increments `bundle_cost[tier]`. Called after each `evaluator(cand)`.\n- **Known-adjacent (do NOT fix):** `Adapter.run` snapshots/digests each artifact payload before domain module can post-process, so predicted cost placed on the payload won''t persist. Must use Bundle/manifest path (which is what was done).\n\n# 3. Artifacts and files\n\n| Path | Role | Status |\n|------|------|--------|\n| `PHASE2.md` (repo root) | Phase 2 status; items 1\u20132 done | **Update pending** |\n| `opensciencelab/base.py` (~308 lines) | `Bundle` dataclass, `Adapter` ABC, `Adapter.run()` | **Modified** \u2014 added `predicted_cost`, `delta_cost` fields to Bundle; added `predict_cost` concrete method to Adapter; `run()` now does pre-flight check \u2192 `_exec` \u2192 charge \u2192 record with predicted/actual/delta |\n| `opensciencelab/manifest.py` (~337 lines) | `Budget` class, `Manifest` class | **Modified** \u2014 added `remaining_for(tier, amount)` method to Budget; extended `Manifest.record()` to accept and store `predicted_cost` and `delta_cost` |\n| `opensciencelab/adapters/optimize/adapter.py` (~507 lines) | `OpenEvolveAdapter` with `_exec` and `_hill_climb` | **Modified** \u2014 added `predict_cost()` method, `charge` closure in `_exec` and `_hill_climb`, real per-tier cost in Bundle, removed hardcoded zeros |\n| `opensciencelab/adapters/scoring.py` (~409 lines) | Tier0/1/2 scoring adapters | **Modified** \u2014 added `predict_cost()` to all four: `Tier0RdkitAdapter`, `Tier1MaceAdapter`, `Tier1ChgnetAdapter`, `Tier2PyscfAdapter` |\n| `opensciencelab/services.py` (224 lines) | `OptimizeService.evolve()` entry; `build_services()` | Read; **not modified** (pre-flight check is in `Adapter.run()`) |\n| `opensciencelab/tests.py` (658 lines, 38 tests) | Full test suite | All 38 pass; **3 new tests pending** |\n| `opensciencelab/drugdiscovery.py` (282 lines) | Drug example; evaluator stamps TIER_ZERO | Read; unchanged |\n| `opensciencelab/materials.py` | Materials example | Grepped; unchanged |\n| `opensciencelab/__init__.py` (72 lines) | Public API, registry | Read; likely no changes needed (no new public symbols) |\n| `scripts/drug_evolve_example.py`, `scripts/materials_evolve_example.py` | Run scripts for proof | **Not yet run** |\n\nWorking directory: `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab`\n\n# 4. Errors and fixes\n\n- **`replace_in_file` failures (multiple instances, base.py and adapter.py):** Stale text matching after prior edits changed the file. Resolved each time by re-reading the relevant lines to get exact current text before constructing the next replacement.\n- **`OptimizeAdapter` vs `OpenEvolveAdapter` in `_rate`:** A grep showed `_DEFAULT_RATE` referenced `OpenEvolveAdapter._DEFAULT_RATE` but a line read showed `OptimizeAdapter._DEFAULT_RATE`. A fix was applied to correct the class name reference.\n- **Duplicated line in admission block:** A `replace_in_file` left a redundant line; caught and removed in a follow-up edit (chars 21220\u219221212).\n- **Adapter class name grep anomaly:** `grep \"^class \\w+\"` on adapter.py returned a blank line at line 44. The actual class is `OpenEvolveAdapter` (confirmed via `__init__.py` registration). The `_rate` static method was fixed to reference the correct class.\n\n# 5. All user messages\n\n1. **(The only user message \u2014 the full task spec):** \"Phase 2, item 3 only. Read PHASE2.md first\u2026 then implement the next open item from Phase 2 of openevolve_roadmap.md \u2014 the budget ledger: every evolve() call reports predicted cost up front and actual cost at the end.\" [Full spec with defect example, current state of all files, 3-part build instructions, constraints, deliverables, proof requirements, and \"then stop.\"]\n\n# 6. Pending tasks\n\n- **Write 3 new tests** at bottom of `opensciencelab/tests.py`:\n  - (a) Call refused up front (prediction > remaining), zero evals performed, `BudgetExceeded` raised.\n  - (b) Run with non-zero recorded cost matching actual evals; `bundle.cost` non-zero and `bundle.predicted_cost` present.\n  - (c) Plateau-killed run: actual < predicted,", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nRecent shell commands:\n- /usr/bin/python3 -c \"import opensciencelab; from opensciencelab.adapters.optimize import adapter; import opensciencelab.tests\" 2>&1 | tail -5  [ok]\n- /usr/bin/python3 -m pytest -q opensciencelab/tests.py 2>&1 | tail -20  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: grep, read_file, replace_in_file, run_shell", "user_messages": ["Phase 2, item 3 only. Read PHASE2.md first (it records items 1\u20132, the defects found, and what is knowingly still broken), then implement the next open item from Phase 2 of openevolve_roadmap.md \u2014 the budget ledger: every evolve() call reports predicted cost up front and actual cost at the end. The defect, from a real run in this repo (runs/*/manifest.json): \"budget\": {\"limits\": {\"1\": 1000.0, \"2\": 500.0}, \"spent\": {\"0\": 0.0, \"1\": 0.0, \"2\": 0.0}} calls[0].cost == {\"0\": 0.0, \"1\": 0.0, \"2\": 0.0} That run did 38 evaluations across 4 generations. The ledger says it cost nothing. Current state \u2014 do \u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787487073.083403, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
