INSERT INTO sessions VALUES('18fd7b24-18a','/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab','ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest','auto','Task: Execute Phase 4 for opensciencelab — the two real fron','builder',375,NULL,'[]',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Phase 4 Drug Materials Pareto',0,'2026-08-26 22:09:39','{}','{"boundary_index": 318, "summary_text": "# 1. Primary request and intent\n\nExecute **Phase 4** of `opensciencelab` (repo at `~/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab`, branch `phase2-drug-and-materials`). Phase 4 is the roadmap exit gate: produce **one real drug-discovery Pareto front** (HCV NS3/4A protease docking, PDB 4K8B) and **one real materials Pareto front** (ABX\u2083 perovskite solar absorbers), both reproducible from manifest alone, plus the 5-section run-report template and the agent loop (brief \u2192 plan \u2192 budget \u2192 run \u2192 report).\n\n**Ordered steps:**\n- Step 0 \u2014 Scope read, confirm 102/102 green \u2705 DONE\n- Step 1 \u2014 Drug front: real NS3/4A receptor PDBQT (4K8B) + real docking Pareto \u2014 **IN PROGRESS** (receptor built; seeding + real run not yet launched)\n- Step 2 \u2014 Materials front: ABX\u2083 perovskite substitution space + CHGNet E_form Pareto \u2014 **BLOCKED** (verify-image chgnet/pymatgen broken; user approved fix)\n- Step 3 \u2014 Run reports (5 sections)\n- Step 4 \u2014 New tests, full suite green, PHASE4.md, request sign-off before close commit\n\n**Standing constraints (permanent, outlive this session):**\n- No new repo dependencies beyond existing optional imports (meeko 0.7.1, gemmi, pyscf, chgnet/pymatgen).\n- `top_n` remains the cost boundary; real kernels only on top-N; KILL-2 monotonic counters tested.\n- `ledger` / `base.py` / `preflight` / `manifest` are **off-limits** unless a root cause genuinely lives there \u2014 stop and ask.\n- Adapter tier honesty (commit `8ae4493`) and KILL-1 stamp-honesty tests must stay green and unweakened; **never edit a stamp to make a test pass**.\n- Seed 1337 pins preserved; provenance in `runs/<id>/manifest.json` for every front.\n- Verify via real-kernel Docker image (`docker/docker-run.sh verify`); fake-kernel tests alone don''t close a Phase-4 run.\n- Stop at every \u2696\ufe0f decision point and wait for user sign-off.\n\n# 2. Key concepts and decisions\n\n- **\u2696\ufe0f Drug front PDB \u2014 CONFIRMED BY USER:** 4K8B (HCV NS3/4A + MK-7009, 1.75 \u00c5, most-cited).\n- **\u2696\ufe0f Materials front \u2014 CONFIRMED BY USER:** Option A \u2014 Full ABX\u2083 substitution space. Cations: MA (CH\u2083NH\u2083), FA (HC(NH\u2082)\u2082), Cs. B-site: Pb, Sn. X-site: I, Br, Cl. Space: **18 compositions**. Band-gap window: **1.5 \u2013 2.2 eV**.\n- **\u2696\ufe0f Verify-image fix \u2014 CONFIRMED BY USER (this session):** \"Fix image: real chgnet from GitHub + pymatgen import robustness.\" The user approved installing chgnet from CederGroupHub GitHub (not the PyPI squatter `0.4.2`) and fixing the pymatgen import.\n- **Zn DROPPED from receptor:** Zn\u2194ligand centroid distance ~25 \u00c5, well outside the 20 \u00c5 box. NS3/4A is a zinc-independent protease.\n- **CRITICAL DISCOVERY \u2014 chgnet PyPI 0.4.2 is a squatter/stub package:** It does NOT expose `StructureRelaxer`, `get_eform_energy`, `get_forces`, or `chgnet.models`. It only has `CHGNet.predict_structure` internals under `chgnet.model.model`. The adapter (`opensciencelab/chgnet.py`) was written against the CederGroupHub API generation. **CHGNet has never run a real call in the verify image.**\n- **CRITICAL DISCOVERY \u2014 pymatgen 2024.9.10 wheel is broken at import:** The full package tree is present (282 .py files, `core/` intact, `from pymatgen.core import Lattice` works) but the **top-level `pymatgen/__init__.py` is missing**, making Python treat it as a namespace package. `from pymatgen import Lattice` fails \u2192 `_HAVE_PYMATGEN = False` in the adapter.\n- **`live_verify.py` result in image:** 5 GREEN / 2 RED. G2 (Vina) GREEN, G4 (PySCF DFT) GREEN, **G3 (CHGNet) RED** \u2014 \"CHGNet/pymatgen not importable.\" The 102/102 test pass is honest (those tests fake-kernel CHGNet), but the real-kernel materials gate was actually red.\n- **Fix plan:** Install real chgnet from CederGroupHub GitHub (`git+https://github.com/CederGroupHub/chgnet@main` or a pinned release tag that ships `StructureRelaxer`/`get_eform_energy`/`get_forces`). Fix pymatgen import in adapter: change `from pymatgen import Lattice, Structure` to `from pymatgen.core import Lattice, Structure` (sub-package import works despite missing top-level `__init__.py`).\n- **`Lattice.cube` \u2192 `Lattice.cubic` API break** (from previous compaction): pymatgen renamed this; adapter''s `_build_structure` may use old name. To be verified after import fix.\n- **CHGNet adapter structure-build gap (UNRESOLVED):** `_build_structure` in `opensciencelab/chgnet.py` builds a 2-atom AB cell (LiF-type). Perovskites are ABX\u2083 (4-atom cubic cell, Pm-3m). **No perovskite path exists** in the codebase. A new structure-builder path for ABX\u2083 is needed for materials front.\n- **PubChem API key correction:** The correct key in PubChem PUG REST JSON response is `ConnectivitySMILES` (NOT `CanonicalSMILES`).\n- **NS3/4A seed panel does NOT exist yet in the repo.** Only generic seeds (aspirin, etc.) in `drugdiscovery.py`. A dedicated NS3/4A inhibitor panel (daclatasvir, etc.) needs to be assembled.\n- **Verify image confirmed:** `opensciencelab:verify` contains: AutoDock Vina 1.2.5, RDKit 2024.03.5, meeko 0.7.1, chgnet (stub), pymatgen (broken import), torch.\n- **Docking seam:** `opensciencelab/docking.py` (274 lines) \u2014 `vina_objective(config)` at line 258. Uses `VINA_RECEPTOR_PDBQT` env var, `VINA_BOX` for box params.\n- **Drug evolve flow:** `scripts/drug_evolve_example.py` (159 lines) \u2192 3-objective Pareto (Vina + QED + SA).\n- **Materials evolve flow:** `scripts/materials_evolve_example.py` (139 lines) \u2192 2-objective (E_form + band gap).\n- **`make_materials_evaluator`** in `opensciencelab/materials.py` line 340: takes `chgnet_fn`, `bg_min` (default 0.8), `bg_max` (default 2.2).\n- **`substitute()`** in `opensciencelab/materials.py` line 243: handles cation/anion substitution.\n- **Dockerfile line 61:** `\"chgnet==0.4.2\"` \u2014 this is the squatter pin to be replaced.\n\n# 3. Artifacts and files\n\n| Path | Role | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `~/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab/` | Main repo, branch `phase2-drug-and-materials` | Active |\n| `data/4K8B.pdb` (1 411 101 bytes) | Raw HCV NS3/4A + MK-7009 crystal structure | Committed |\n| `data/4K8B_receptor.pdbqt` | Chain-A receptor, 1 609 ATOM lines, RIGID, no HETATM | Built, verified |\n| `data/4K8B_meta.json` | Metadata: vina_box (center on 1RR centroid, size 20 \u00c5), `kept_zinc: 0`, `charge_model: gasteiger` | Written |\n| `scripts/make_receptor_4k8b.py` | Pre-filters chain A, `meeko.Polymer.from_pdb_string` + `residues_to_delete`, `parameterize(rigid=True)`. Box size 20 \u00c5. | Final working version |\n| `opensciencelab/docking.py` (274 lines) | Vina adapter + `vina_objective()`. Lines 258-265: `vina_objective` returns lambda wrapping `VinaAdapter.dock`. | Read, understood |\n| `opensciencelab/chgnet.py` (549 lines) | CHGNet E_form adapter. Lines 80-84: import guard `_HAVE_CHGNET`. Lines 86-87: pymatgen import guard `_HAVE_PYMATGEN`. Line 201: `_build_structure` (2-atom AB cell only \u2014 **NO perovskite path**). Line 228: `_run_chgnet`. Line 379: `evaluate()`. | Read; gaps identified |\n| `opensciencelab/materials.py` (537 lines) | `substitute()` (line 243), `make_materials_evaluator()` (line 340) with `bg_min`/`bg_max`/`bg_width` params. | Read; understood |\n| `scripts/drug_evolve_example.py` (159 lines) | Drug evolve entry: 3-objective Pareto (Vina + QED + SA). | Read |\n| `scripts/materials_evolve_example.py` (139 lines) | Materials evolve entry: 2-objective (E_form + band gap). | Referenced |\n| `opensciencelab/report.py` (162 lines) | 5-section markdown report renderer. | Referenced |\n| `docker/docker-run.sh` (79 lines) | Docker run wrapper for Strix Halo gfx1151. GPU flags. | Read |\n| `opensciencelab/drugdiscovery.py` | Generic seed defaults (aspirin, etc.) \u2014 **no NS3/4A-specific seeds**. | Read |\n| `opensciencelab/tests.py` (2544 lines) | Full test suite. Lines 2100+: CHGNet tests (fake-kernel). | Read (spot) |\n| `Dockerfile` (115 lines) | Lines 55-61: pip install block with `chgnet==0.4.2` (squatter) and `pymatgen==2024.9.10`. Lines 99-114: healthcheck. | Read; needs chgnet pin fix |\n| `scripts/live_verify.py` (410 lines) | Real-kernel G1-G4 exit gate. Line 201: `_row_chgnet()`. | Read; G3 RED |\n| `PHASE3.md` | Phase 3 closeout doc. | Referenced |\n| `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/knowledge/threads/opensciencelab-phase-4.md` | Brain note: Phase 4 blocker diagnosis. | Written |\n\n# 4. Errors and fixes\n\n- **CHGNet G3 gate RED in verify image:**\n  - Root cause 1: `chgnet==0", "working_state": "## Working state (extracted mechanically from tool records)\nRecent shell commands:\n- docker run --rm opensciencelab:verify sh -c \" P=/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/chgnet echo ''=== def get_eform_energy / get_forces / StructureRelaxer ==  [ok]\n- docker run --rm -v /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab:/repo -w /repo opensciencelab:verify sh -c \" cd /tmp && pip install --no-deps ''chgn  [ok]\n- docker run --rm opensciencelab:verify python3 -c \" # Try the exact imports the adapter uses try: from chgnet import StructureRelaxer, get_eform_energy, get_forc  [ok]\n- docker run --rm opensciencelab:verify sh -c \" P=/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/chgnet echo ''=== where are formation/bandgap/e_form computed? ==='' grep   [ok]\n- docker run --rm opensciencelab:verify python3 -c \" import chgnet print(''chgnet __version__ ='', getattr(chgnet, ''__version__'', ''MISSING'')) print() import opensci  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab cat > /tmp/p4/flags.py <<''PY'' print(''--- import diagnostics (fresh process) ---'') # 1) raw top-leve  [ok]\n- cd /home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab cat > /tmp/p4/pm.py <<''PY'' import pymatgen, os print(\"pymatgen.__file__ =\", getattr(pymatgen, \"__fi  [ok]\n- docker run --rm opensciencelab:verify sh -c \" echo ''=== contents of pymatgen/ package dir ==='' ls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pymatgen/ 2>&1 | h  [ok]\n- docker run --rm opensciencelab:verify sh -c \" echo ''=== core/__init__.py ? ==='' ls /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pymatgen/core/__init__.py 2>&1 echo e  [ok]\n- cd /tmp && rm -rf chgchk && mkdir chgchk && cd chgchk for v in 0.3.8 0.4.0; do curl -fsSL -o cnet$v.whl https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/$(curl -fsSL \"ht  [ok]\nTools used in the summarized span: ask_user, brain_note, brain_recall, grep, read_file, run_shell, todo_write", "user_messages": ["Task: Execute Phase 4 for opensciencelab \u2014 the two real fronts (drug + materials) and their run reports Repo: ~/openworker-workspace/opensciencelab, branch phase2-drug-and-materials, baseline commit 3ef8030 (Phase 3 closed 2026-08-25, 102/102 tests). Read PHASE3.md (esp. the closure report \u00a75 and \"Step 4 decisions\") and PHASE2.md before touching code. Roadmap: ~/openworker-workspace/openevolve_roadmap.md. What Phase 4 is: the roadmap exit gate \u2014 \"one real drug-discovery Pareto front AND one real materials Pareto front, both reproducible from manifest alone.\" The Phase-3 seams are proven; Phas\u2026", "4H5F HCV NS3/4A + MK-7009, 1.75 \u00c5, most-cited crystallographic reference Canonical active geometry, large community, well-trodden docking baselines Has an inhibitor in the active site \u2014 must be stripped, which changes the active-site conformation slightly from the apo state Option A \u2014 Full ABX\u2083 substitution space (roadmap as stated): Cations: MA (CH\u2083NH\u2083), FA (HC(NH\u2082)\u2082), Cs \u2014 3 B-site: Pb, Sn \u2014 2 X-site: I, Br, Cl \u2014 3 Space: 3 \u00d7 2 \u00d7 3 = 18 compositions Band-gap window: 1.5 \u2013 2.2 eV (solar absorber range) CHGNet kernel: the current adapter''s _build_structure returns a 2-atom AB cell \u2014 I will ne\u2026"], "user_messages_dropped": 0, "created_at": 1787779477.0279715, "model_used": "ollama:qwen3.8-27b:latest", "trimmed": false}');
